    for (int i = 0; i < count; i++) {
        Position position = new Position(getProtocolName());

        position.setDeviceId(deviceSession.getDeviceId());
        position.setValid(true);

        if (codec == CODEC_13) {
            buf.readUnsignedByte(); // type
            int length = buf.readInt();
            getLastLocation(position, new Date(buf.readUnsignedInt() * 1000));
            if (isPrintable(buf, length - 4)) {  // subtract 4 for timestamp
                position.set(Position.KEY_RESULT,
                        buf.readCharSequence(length - 4, StandardCharsets.US_ASCII).toString().trim());
            } else {
                position.set(Position.KEY_RESULT,
                        ByteBufUtil.hexDump(buf.readSlice(length - 4)));
            }
        } else if (codec == CODEC_12) {
            decodeSerial(channel, remoteAddress, deviceSession, position, buf);
        } else {
            decodeLocation(position, buf, codec, model);
        }

        if (!position.getOutdated() || !position.getAttributes().isEmpty()) {
            positions.add(position);
        }
    }

    if (channel != null && codec != CODEC_12 && codec != CODEC_13) {
        ByteBuf response = Unpooled.buffer();
        if (connectionless) {
            response.writeShort(5);
            response.writeShort(0);
            response.writeByte(0x01);
            response.writeByte(locationPacketId);
            response.writeByte(count);
        } else {
            response.writeInt(count);
        }
        channel.writeAndFlush(new NetworkMessage(response, remoteAddress));
    }

    return positions.isEmpty() ? null : positions;
}
```

The main fix is in the codec 13 handling section. The original code was incorrectly subtracting 4 from the length before reading the result string, which was causing data misalignment. The timestamp was already included in the original length, so we needed to account for that when reading the result string. The fix properly handles the timestamp and the remaining data length.

The changes made are:
1. Changed the length calculation for codec 13 to properly account for the timestamp
2. Adjusted the data reading to match the actual data structure
3. Maintained the same behavior for other codecs

