The key fix is in the `case 0xFE` block. Previously, if `length` was greater than 1, it was skipping setting the battery level before reading the mark byte. I've moved the `position.set(Position.KEY_BATTERY_LEVEL, buf.readUnsignedByte());` line to be executed in both cases, which fixes the battery level reading.

This change ensures that the battery level is always set when processing the 0xFE subtype, regardless of the length value, which should fix the test case that was failing.

